<p>Decimal 36865. Default value: 38 (PAL), 25 (NTSC). Also known as <strong>VICCR1</strong>.</p>
<p>The distance from the top of the TV picture to the first row of characters.
Changing it moves the whole display up or down, which can be used for a cheap
vertical scroll or a screen shake.</p>
<p>Note that the value counts in half raster lines, so each step of 1 moves the
display two scan lines.</p>

<p>Example</p>
<code>
// bounce the screen up and down
VSCROLL_REGISTER := 38 + (frame &amp; 1);
</code>
<p>See also HSCROLL_REGISTER ($9000) for the horizontal equivalent.</p>
